# ===== 06Exp LowPa: Cattaneo et al. (Nat. Phys. 2025) EXPERIMENTAL CONFIGURATION, full 3D bubble under a rigid substrate
# Purpose: jetting and non-spherical shape modes, which the symmetric octant cannot show.
# Experiment (paper Methods + Fig. 1b, 2): HUVEC cells on a rigid PLASTIC substrate; the microbubble floats up and
#   rests against a cell, so the substrate is ABOVE the bubble.  The paper's translation model puts the rigid plastic
#   at L ~ 12 um from the bubble centre (cell thickness, Methods eq. 5); the soft cell layer between is negligible for
#   the acoustics (paper: its contribution to the secondary Bjerknes force is negligible).
# Here: bubble centre at the origin, NO-SLIP NO-PENETRATION wall at z = +3.70 um (the top face, REFLECT_ODD momentum).
#   2026-11-19: the wall stands in for the CELL SURFACE the bubble rests on (was the plastic at 12 um, stand-off ~4:
#   too weak a wall asymmetry to jet).  The cell is acoustically transparent but the liquid cannot flow through it, so
#   the near-field boundary is the cell surface.  Gap bubble-wall = 0.60 um = 2.6 eps (eta at the wall 0.995 at t = 0),
#   stand-off 1.19.  Box moved down 8.30 um relative to the bubble (same size, grid and cubic cells).
# Drive: ONE focused transducer (PA1280, 1 MHz, -6 dB beam ~3 mm) from BELOW at 75 deg to the horizontal.  The box
#   (~120 um) is << the wavelength (1.48 mm) and << the beam, so at the bubble the incident + wall-reflected field is a
#   spatially uniform oscillation (rigid wall = pressure antinode, dp/dz = 0; cos(kz) > 0.98 over the box).  The paper's
#   p_a is the amplitude fitted at the bubble (it absorbs the reflections), so the same p_d(t) is imposed on the FIVE
#   open faces (xlo, xhi, ylo, yhi, zlo) with the spherical radiation condition centred on the bubble.  Neglected: the
#   travelling-wave gradient (primary Bjerknes p ~ (4/3) R k p_a ~ 3 kPa << p_a), small in the paper's Fig. 2e budget.
# Everything else (shell, gas, water, Option 1 relaxation, conduction dt, AMR layout) is identical to
#   input_06_Cattaneo_LowPa, so the octant and this run differ only by the substrate and the symmetry.
# Stop at 10.5 us: the experimental record ends at t_fig = 12.0 us = t_sim 10.43 us.
#
# MarmPaper 06: VALIDATION against Cattaneo et al., Nature Physics 21:590 (2025), Fig. 2a (low p_a)
#
# Same ICs as the paper (their code: github.com/cttnmrc/jetting-enables-sonoporation):
#   R0 = 3.10 um (2026-11-11: the paper's 60 kPa model line and the 60 kPa experiment bubble use 3.10 um; was 2.95), water rho 997.8, c 1481 m/s, mu 0.954e-3, p0 = 102200 Pa, T = 295 K;
#   Marmottant shell chi 0.15 N/m, kappa_s 5e-9 kg/s, sigma(R0) = 0 (R_buckling = R0), rupture at 0.0728 N/m;
#   1 MHz drive, amplitude p_a = 60 kPa (their nominal), with the MEASURED pulse envelope
#   (nscbc.drive_envelope; burst 0..40 us).  Gas-liquid heat transfer ON (their Zhou gas model is
#   heat conducting; Pe = w R0^2/D ~ 2.5, near-isothermal).
#   Cross-law shell viscosity ON (shell.kappa_s_alpha = 4e-6; remedy b).  The paper uses CONSTANT kappa_s:
#   run with shell.kappa_s_alpha=0 on the command line for the paper's shell model.
# TIME AXIS: the burst starts at t = 0 here; their Fig. 2 axis has it at ~2 us (figure t = t + 2 us).
# Their spherical model (Python port, ~/claude_scratch/papers/port_cattaneo.py) with this envelope gives
#   high p_a peaks 3.49 3.82 4.03 4.21 4.39 4.59 4.79 5.02 5.29 um in pulse cycles 1..9 (constant kappa_s);
#   Cross law: 3.56 3.97 4.19 4.39 4.70 5.20 5.95 6.70 6.94 um.  Measured (their Fig. 2a): ~3.55 4.15 4.25
#   4.35 4.45 4.6 4.7 4.95 5.1 um.
# DIFFERENCES from the experiment: free bubble (octant, no cell/substrate), so no translation, no
#   wall-driven jets; their bubble rests on a cell.  Box gain ~1 (20 R0 box << wavelength).
# stop_time = 12 us (pulse time).
#
# COMMON: RK3 + MUSCL2 + HLLC, cfl 0.9, eps/dx_finest = 2, R0/dx_finest = 25.6 (max_level 4), NSCBC far field.
alamo.program = hydro2
plot_file = /mmfs1/home/ttryon/flames/bin/tests/FlowMarmottant/MarmPaper/output_06Exp_Cattaneo_LowPa

### OUTPUT ###
amr.plot_int       = -1
amr.plot_dt        = 5.000000e-08    # 20 frames/us (2x their camera); full-sphere plotfiles are ~8x the octant size
amr.thermo.plot_dt = 1.000000e-09    # thermo.dat: gas_volume (R_vol), gas_pressure_int, kinetic_energy, interface_area
plot_minimal       = 1

### MESH ###
amr.max_grid_size  = 8    # 2026-11-14: was 16 (measured with blocking_factor 8, 8 ranks: 25 -> 103 finest boxes, 1.7x faster); allows 64 tasks
amr.blocking_factor = 8    # 2026-11-14: was 16 (measured: finest cells 110592 -> 52736, 1.5x faster; 4 gives no further gain)
amr.regrid_int     = 10
amr.grid_eff       = 0.8
amr.max_level      = 4
amr.n_error_buf    = 4   # 2026-11-10: was 16 (2.4x fewer finest cells, 1.9x faster; band still tagged by grad eta)
nghost = 4

### GEOMETRY -- OCTANT (active); full domain below, commented ###
geometry.prob_lo     = -5.900000e-05 -5.900000e-05 -7.005000e-05
geometry.prob_hi     = 5.900000e-05 5.900000e-05 3.700000e-06   # top face = rigid substrate, 3.70 um above the bubble centre (gap 0.60 um = 2.6 eps)
geometry.is_periodic = 0 0 0
amr.n_cell           = 64 64 40     # base dx 1.84375e-06 in all directions; finest dx 1.1523e-07 (R0/dx 25.6)
# --- full domain (swap with the octant block above; also swap the BC block) ---
# geometry.prob_lo     = -5.900000e-05 -5.900000e-05 -5.900000e-05
# geometry.prob_hi     = 5.900000e-05 5.900000e-05 5.900000e-05
# geometry.is_periodic = 0 0 0
# amr.n_cell           = 64 64 64

### TIME ###
timestep                = 1.0e-12
dynamictimestep.on      = 1
dynamictimestep.verbose = 0
dynamictimestep.max     = 1.0e-9
dynamictimestep.min     = 1.0e-18
cfl                     = 0.9
stop_time               = 1.050000e-05    # experiment record ends at t_sim 10.43 us

### INTERFACE ###
eta.ic.type = expression
eta.ic.expression.constant.epsilon = 2.304688e-07    # eps/dx_finest = 2
eta.ic.expression.constant.R0      = 3.100000e-06
eta.ic.expression.region0 = "0.5*(1 + tanh((sqrt(x*x + y*y + z*z) - R0)/epsilon))"
epsilon = eta.ic.expression.constant.epsilon

### EOS: 0 = water (stiffened gas), 1 = perfluorobutane C4F10 (Cattaneo core gas) ###
eos0.gamma = 2.35
eos0.p0    = 9.311895e+08   # c_water = 1481 m/s at rho 997.8 (paper)
eos0.cv    = 2343.6161      # calibrated: T_water = 295 K at p0
eos0.cp    = 5507.4978      # = gamma cv
eos1.gamma = 1.07       # C4F10: M 238.03 g/mol, Rg 34.93 J/kg/K (was air 1.4)
eos1.p0    = 0.0
eos1.cv    = 499.0      # Rg/(gamma-1)
eos1.cp    = 533.9      # gamma cv

### INITIAL CONDITIONS ###
density0.ic.type = expression
density0.ic.expression.region0 = "997.8"
density1.ic.type = expression
density1.ic.expression.region0 = "9.918"         # C4F10 ideal gas at p0 = 102200 Pa and 295 K
velocity0.ic.type = expression
velocity0.ic.expression.region0 = "0.0"
velocity0.ic.expression.region1 = "0.0"
velocity0.ic.expression.region2 = "0.0"
velocity1.ic.type = expression
velocity1.ic.expression.region0 = "0.0"
velocity1.ic.expression.region1 = "0.0"
velocity1.ic.expression.region2 = "0.0"
pressure0.ic.type = expression
pressure0.ic.expression.constant.p_inf = 1.022000e+05
pressure0.ic.expression.constant.p_b   = 1.022000e+05
pressure0.ic.expression.constant.R0    = 3.100000e-06
pressure0.ic.expression.region0 = "p_inf"
pressure1.ic.type = expression
pressure1.ic.expression.constant.p_b = 1.022000e+05      # sigma(R0) = 0: gas at p0
pressure1.ic.expression.region0 = "p_b"
equalize_ic_pressure = 1

### MATERIAL / SHELL ###
mu0   = 9.5400e-04   # water (paper)
mu0_b = 0.0
mu1   = 0.0
mu1_b = 0.0
apply_surface_tension = 1
sigma = 0.0728                   # water (= post-rupture tension)
pref  = 0.0
marmottant             = 1
marmottant.R0          = 3.100000e-06  # shell unstrained at the IC radius
marmottant.R_buckling  = 3.100000e-06  # = R0: sigma(R0) = 0, starts at buckling (paper)
marmottant.chi         = 0.15          # [N/m] (paper)
marmottant.sigma_break = 0.0728        # [N/m] rupture at the water tension (paper: S_w)
shell.kappa_s = 5.0e-9                  # [kg/s] (paper)
shell.kappa_s_alpha = 0.0               # [s] constant kappa_s as in the paper (base deck: 4e-6 Cross law)
shell.slip          = 12                # Gamma = m/|grad psi| (see Hydro2 Parse)
face.two_pressure   = 1                 # option 10: face rebuild keeps gas at its own pressure
relax.opt8          = 1                 # option 8=1: trace gas keeps its own energy
relax.trace_pT      = 3                 # trace gas frozen below the cutoff (fixes cold gas, 2026-11-12)
thermal.alpha_min   = 1.0e-4
nscbc.spherical     = 1                 # spherical (Bayliss-Turkel) radiation condition; plane wave rejected
thermal.dt_limit    = 1                 # conduction diffusion limit in dt (default 1; fixes fine-grid NaN at max expansion)
visc.relax_cell_local = 0               # 0 = viscous relaxation jump integrated along grad eta in the band (Option 1, default); 1 = old per-cell
shell.mu_s    = 0.0

### BOUNDARY CONDITIONS -- full domain: rigid substrate (zhi) + 5 driven NSCBC faces ###
# Drive: p_target(t) = p_inf + drive_amp sin(drive_omega t) * envelope on every NSCBC face (measured pulse envelope,
# applied exactly as the paper's MATLAB).  Spherical radiation condition centred on the bubble (origin).
nscbc.drive_envelope = ./tests/FlowMarmottant/MarmPaper/reference/cattaneo2025_envelope.dat
nscbc.drive_t0       = 0.0
nscbc.drive_center   = 0.0 0.0 0.0
nscbc.xlo.type     = outflow
nscbc.xlo.target_p = 1.022000e+05
nscbc.xlo.sigma    = 0.6
nscbc.xlo.beta     = 0.5
nscbc.xlo.L_ref    = 1.843750e-07
nscbc.xlo.drive_amp   = 5.390000e+04   # C4F10 refit p_a (2026-11-19; paper air fit was 6.000000e+04)
nscbc.xlo.drive_omega = 6.283185e+06
nscbc.xhi.type     = outflow
nscbc.xhi.target_p = 1.022000e+05
nscbc.xhi.sigma    = 0.6
nscbc.xhi.beta     = 0.5
nscbc.xhi.L_ref    = 1.843750e-07
nscbc.xhi.drive_amp   = 5.390000e+04   # C4F10 refit p_a (2026-11-19; paper air fit was 6.000000e+04)
nscbc.xhi.drive_omega = 6.283185e+06
nscbc.ylo.type     = outflow
nscbc.ylo.target_p = 1.022000e+05
nscbc.ylo.sigma    = 0.6
nscbc.ylo.beta     = 0.5
nscbc.ylo.L_ref    = 1.843750e-07
nscbc.ylo.drive_amp   = 5.390000e+04   # C4F10 refit p_a (2026-11-19; paper air fit was 6.000000e+04)
nscbc.ylo.drive_omega = 6.283185e+06
nscbc.yhi.type     = outflow
nscbc.yhi.target_p = 1.022000e+05
nscbc.yhi.sigma    = 0.6
nscbc.yhi.beta     = 0.5
nscbc.yhi.L_ref    = 1.843750e-07
nscbc.yhi.drive_amp   = 5.390000e+04   # C4F10 refit p_a (2026-11-19; paper air fit was 6.000000e+04)
nscbc.yhi.drive_omega = 6.283185e+06
nscbc.zlo.type     = outflow
nscbc.zlo.target_p = 1.022000e+05
nscbc.zlo.sigma    = 0.6
nscbc.zlo.beta     = 0.5
nscbc.zlo.L_ref    = 1.843750e-07
nscbc.zlo.drive_amp   = 5.390000e+04   # C4F10 refit p_a (2026-11-19; paper air fit was 6.000000e+04)
nscbc.zlo.drive_omega = 6.283185e+06
nscbc.zhi.type     = none     # rigid substrate (no NSCBC)
eta.bc.type.xlo = neumann
eta.bc.type.xhi = neumann
eta.bc.type.ylo = neumann
eta.bc.type.yhi = neumann
eta.bc.type.zlo = neumann
eta.bc.type.zhi = REFLECT_EVEN
eta.contact_angle.zhi = 0     # wall wetting (2026-11-19): contact angle through the liquid [deg]; the hydrogel/cell
                              # surface is water-saturated and hydrophilic, so water wets it and a liquid film stays
                              # between gas and wall (0 = complete wetting).  Unset = mirror ghosts = 90 deg (neutral).
density.bc.type.xlo = nscbc_outflow
density.bc.type.xhi = nscbc_outflow
density.bc.type.ylo = nscbc_outflow
density.bc.type.yhi = nscbc_outflow
density.bc.type.zlo = nscbc_outflow
density.bc.type.zhi = REFLECT_EVEN
energy.bc.type.xlo = nscbc_outflow
energy.bc.type.xhi = nscbc_outflow
energy.bc.type.ylo = nscbc_outflow
energy.bc.type.yhi = nscbc_outflow
energy.bc.type.zlo = nscbc_outflow
energy.bc.type.zhi = REFLECT_EVEN
momentum.bc.type.xlo = nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow
momentum.bc.type.xhi = nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow
momentum.bc.type.ylo = nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow
momentum.bc.type.yhi = nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow
momentum.bc.type.zlo = nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow nscbc_outflow
momentum.bc.type.zhi = REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_ODD   # no-slip, no-penetration wall: u = 0 on the face

eta_refinement_criterion   = 1.0e-1
omega_refinement_criterion = 1.0e+10
p_refinement_criterion     = 1.0e+10
rho_refinement_criterion   = 1.0e+10
gradu_refinement_criterion = 1.0e+10

### NUMERICS ###
cutoff = 1.0e-4
Riemann_Solver.type = hllc
Limiter.type        = muscl2
# THINC qq (second round; uncomment these three lines and comment out Limiter.type above):
# Limiter.type       = thinc
# Limiter.thinc.thinc_base = muscl2
# Limiter.thinc.thinc_mode = qq       # key is Limiter.thinc.<key> (Limiter.thinc_mode is silently ignored)
integration.type    = RungeKutta
integration.rk.type = 3
visc_subcycle              = 1       # bulk + shell viscous terms sub-cycled
visc.flux_form             = 1       # bulk viscous stress as conservative face fluxes (harmonic face mu); the old expanded form
                                     # mu lap(u) + grad(mu).grad(u) runs away in light band-tail cells at fine dx (2D jet crash 2026-11-19)
shell.kappa_s_subcycle_max = 8192
shell.heat_split           = 2       # shell viscous heat split by thermal effusivity
shell.foot_rate            = 1       # viscous-jump rate and curvature taken at the foot point on eta = 1/2 (fixes the axis-tip runaway, see Hydro2 Parse)
thermal.k0                 = 0.6     # water [W/m/K]
thermal.k1                 = 0.012   # C4F10 [W/m/K]
thermal.conduction         = 1       # Fourier conduction in each phase (2026-11-10: micro bubbles are
thermal.exchange           = 1       #   near-isothermal, Pe = w R^2/D ~ 2-16; adiabatic gas is too stiff)
relax_diag                 = 0
apply_weight          = 0
apply_vaporization    = 0
grav                  = 0.0
m0.ic.constant.value = 0.0
u0.ic.constant.value = 0.0 0.0
q.ic.constant.value  = 0.0 0.0
